// Claim filing and instruction (D.262-26/27/28/29/30).
//
// DEONTIC MAP:
// - D.262-26 "peut être déposée" is five claimant liberties, one per
//   venue, each with its article condition (board decision, delegation,
//   France Travail empowerment); the 2024-07-01 Pôle emploi rename is
//   read and immaterial to the norms (single rules spanning the whole
//   window, predecessor fragments cited);
// - D.262-27 al.1 is the France Travail board liberty to take on
//   instruction; al.2 (modalities fixed by convention) gates the
//   institutional empowerment ft_habilite_instruire, which enables the
//   D.262-26 e) venue; the convention's conclusion itself is an
//   inter-institutional act arriving established;
// - D.262-28 gratuitous instruction is two prohibitions (body, department
//   services) on charging, each bound to the service/body that received
//   the filing (« auprès desquels elles ont été déposées »); an
//   instructor that did not receive the filing owes nothing;
// - D.262-29 joint quality engagement is two mirror duties (body side,
//   president side) toward the claimant;
// - D.262-30 delegation scope is the president's duty to fix the
//   territorial scope in the delegation.

language "law.core" version "0.2";
package fr.casf.rsa version "0.1.0";
namespace "urn:fr:corpus:clir:rsa";

// `use self` is hand-maintained in nochecks authoring (no `law fix
// imports` until the locks free). Fragment names join the block via the
// deferred `law fix imports fr.casf.rsa` run after regenerating sources.
use self::{
    CASF_D262_26,
    CASF_D262_26_ED2025_01,
    CASF_D262_26_ED2025_06,
